WEBVTT

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:01.390
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.554 --> 00:00:06.350
In this lesson, we build extensions with builder gel on forms, step by step.

00:00:06.674 --> 00:00:08.510
Keep in mind three things throughout:

00:00:08.779 --> 00:00:13.710
the form snug and straight, no gel on the skin, and the apex in the right place.

00:00:14.287 --> 00:00:15.004
Step one:

00:00:15.254 --> 00:00:16.764
consultation and check.

00:00:17.335 --> 00:00:20.684
Wash and sanitize your hands, and the hands of the client.

00:00:21.188 --> 00:00:23.724
Look closely at the nails and the skin around them.

00:00:24.152 --> 00:00:29.628
If a nail is separating from the bed or discolored, or the skin is red, swollen,

00:00:29.578 --> 00:00:31.324
has pus or an open wound,

00:00:31.593 --> 00:00:35.084
do not do the service, and advise the client to see a doctor.

00:00:35.265 --> 00:00:37.816
Ask whether the client has ever had itching,

00:00:37.766 --> 00:00:40.204
redness or blistering after a gel service.

00:00:40.556 --> 00:00:43.522
Then choose the length and shape together with the client,

00:00:43.472 --> 00:00:45.884
to suit the natural nails and their daily work.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.684
For a first set, choose a moderate length.

00:00:48.896 --> 00:00:51.884
Once the client is used to it, the next set can be longer.

00:00:52.073 --> 00:00:53.084
And tell them up front:

00:00:53.297 --> 00:00:56.284
they should come back for an infill in about three to four weeks.

00:00:56.831 --> 00:00:57.723
Step two:

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:01.243
dry prep, as in the gel polish and builder gel lessons.

00:01:01.746 --> 00:01:06.689
Push back the cuticle, buff lightly to remove the shine, brush off the dust,

00:01:06.639 --> 00:01:08.363
cleanse, and from then on,

00:01:08.462 --> 00:01:10.203
do not touch the nail surface.

00:01:10.631 --> 00:01:13.973
File the natural free edge short and neat, but leave a little,

00:01:13.923 --> 00:01:16.203
so the form has something to rest against.

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:17.661
Step three:

00:01:17.986 --> 00:01:19.101
prepare the form.

00:01:19.738 --> 00:01:22.541
Peel the form off, and try it under the free edge.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:26.897
If the curve of the form does not match the free edge, trim it to fit,

00:01:26.847 --> 00:01:29.341
so the form sits snugly under the free edge,

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:30.221
with no gap.

00:01:30.883 --> 00:01:31.747
Step four:

00:01:31.929 --> 00:01:32.867
fit the form.

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:37.427
Slide the form under the free edge, and push it snug, with no gap.

00:01:37.853 --> 00:01:38.946
Then look from above:

00:01:39.373 --> 00:01:42.307
the form is in line with the finger, centered on the nail.

00:01:42.651 --> 00:01:43.507
Look from the tip:

00:01:43.856 --> 00:01:46.627
the form is level, not tilted to either side.

00:01:47.026 --> 00:01:47.987
Look from the side:

00:01:48.327 --> 00:01:52.867
the form continues the line of the nail, not pointing down, not pointing up.

00:01:53.035 --> 00:01:57.146
When it is right, pinch the tails of the form together under the finger,

00:01:57.096 --> 00:01:58.387
so the form stays put.

00:01:58.916 --> 00:02:00.394
One form per finger.

00:02:00.711 --> 00:02:03.274
When you are learning, do one finger at a time:

00:02:03.453 --> 00:02:07.914
fit the form, build the extension, cure, and only then move on.

00:02:08.481 --> 00:02:12.634
Once your hands are used to it, you can fit forms on several fingers at once.

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:14.919
The thumb is usually done separately,

00:02:14.869 --> 00:02:17.352
because it sits at an angle to the other fingers,

00:02:17.302 --> 00:02:19.834
and is hard to get into the lamp at the same time.

00:02:20.479 --> 00:02:21.365
Step five:

00:02:21.628 --> 00:02:23.285
a very thin base layer.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:27.833
Take a little gel, press and scrub it gently into the nail surface,

00:02:27.783 --> 00:02:31.205
remove the excess, and leave a fine line from the skin.

00:02:31.636 --> 00:02:35.845
Then cure it, or leave it uncured, exactly as the brand instructs.

00:02:36.484 --> 00:02:37.464
Step six:

00:02:37.642 --> 00:02:39.304
build the extension on the form.

00:02:39.621 --> 00:02:43.602
Take some gel, place it just in front of the edge of the natural nail,

00:02:43.552 --> 00:02:45.624
then spread it thinly over the form,

00:02:45.817 --> 00:02:47.464
to make the long part of the nail.

00:02:47.893 --> 00:02:50.344
This part must join the edge of the natural nail.

00:02:50.695 --> 00:02:53.064
Create the length and the tip shape right now:

00:02:53.333 --> 00:02:56.824
the side walls straight, continuing the sides of the natural nail.

00:02:57.173 --> 00:02:59.464
Gel must not run over the edge of the form.

00:02:59.628 --> 00:03:02.024
This layer is thin, just a foundation.

00:03:02.293 --> 00:03:04.024
The strength comes from the overlay.

00:03:04.331 --> 00:03:06.904
When done, cure for the time the brand gives.

00:03:07.555 --> 00:03:08.423
Step seven:

00:03:08.729 --> 00:03:10.423
the overlay and the apex.

00:03:10.881 --> 00:03:15.303
Place a bead of gel on the stress area, where the natural nail leaves the skin bed.

00:03:15.718 --> 00:03:18.103
Gently guide the gel towards the cuticle,

00:03:18.053 --> 00:03:21.063
and stop with a gap as thin as a hair from the skin.

00:03:21.486 --> 00:03:26.023
Then guide it out to the sides, and over the whole extension, capping the free edge.

00:03:26.451 --> 00:03:31.223
The gel is thin at the cuticle, thin at the tip, and fullest over the stress area.

00:03:31.753 --> 00:03:35.989
Turn the hand of the client palm down, and hold it still for a few seconds,

00:03:35.939 --> 00:03:38.111
so the gel settles towards the middle,

00:03:38.185 --> 00:03:39.471
into a soft curve.

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:42.511
Then turn it back up, and look from the side:

00:03:42.853 --> 00:03:45.071
the highest point sits over the stress area.

00:03:45.563 --> 00:03:46.431
Look from the tip:

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:48.991
the C curve is even on both sides.

00:03:49.339 --> 00:03:52.271
Fix anything that is not right while the gel is still wet.

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:56.831
Then cure for the full time, and wipe off the sticky layer if the product has one.

00:03:57.478 --> 00:03:58.275
Step eight:

00:03:58.448 --> 00:03:59.555
remove the form.

00:03:59.955 --> 00:04:03.871
Loosen the tails of the form a little, then pull the form downwards,

00:04:03.821 --> 00:04:05.235
away from the free edge.

00:04:05.584 --> 00:04:07.395
Do not bend it backwards and up.

00:04:07.741 --> 00:04:09.635
Look at the underside of the extension:

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:13.715
it must be flat, clean, and joined to the natural nail.

00:04:14.213 --> 00:04:19.137
If there is a ridge of gel underneath, or gel stuck to the skin under the free edge,

00:04:19.087 --> 00:04:20.355
file it gently clean,

00:04:20.466 --> 00:04:22.595
and fit the form more snugly next time.

00:04:23.264 --> 00:04:24.118
Step nine:

00:04:24.299 --> 00:04:24.998
filing.

00:04:25.304 --> 00:04:28.118
Switch on the dust extraction, and put on a mask.

00:04:28.386 --> 00:04:30.118
Use a 180 grit file.

00:04:30.387 --> 00:04:35.078
File the tip into the right shape, and file the side walls straight and parallel.

00:04:35.509 --> 00:04:40.088
Then lay the file flat on the nail surface, and file it smooth and even,

00:04:40.038 --> 00:04:41.158
keeping the apex.

00:04:41.587 --> 00:04:46.117
At the cuticle, file lightly to thin it, so it blends into the natural nail,

00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:48.358
but do not file into the natural nail.

00:04:48.591 --> 00:04:51.878
Brush the dust away, do not blow it, then cleanse.

00:04:52.401 --> 00:04:54.288
Look again from three directions:

00:04:54.318 --> 00:04:57.168
from the side, from the tip, and from above.

00:04:57.618 --> 00:04:59.168
The nails must all match:

00:04:59.197 --> 00:05:04.288
the same length, the same shape, and the apex moderately high over the stress area.

00:05:04.713 --> 00:05:09.860
If an apex is low, or one side is thicker than the other, correct it with the file,

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:11.088
or add a thin layer,

00:05:11.237 --> 00:05:12.928
cure, and file again.

00:05:13.608 --> 00:05:14.387
Step ten:

00:05:14.654 --> 00:05:15.907
color and finish.

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:20.467
If the client likes a natural look, one coat of glossy top coat is enough.

00:05:20.736 --> 00:05:25.587
If she wants color, paint colored gel very thinly, as in the gel polish lesson.

00:05:26.016 --> 00:05:29.747
The top coat caps the edge of the tip, then cure for the full time.

00:05:30.255 --> 00:05:35.347
Finally, put a drop of cuticle oil on the skin around the nails, and massage gently.

00:05:35.978 --> 00:05:36.886
Tell the client:

00:05:37.059 --> 00:05:40.326
do not pick at them, and do not use your nails as tools.

00:05:40.729 --> 00:05:42.966
Wear gloves when washing up or cleaning.

00:05:43.534 --> 00:05:46.806
For the first few days, the client needs to get used to the new length:

00:05:47.131 --> 00:05:50.966
be careful opening car doors, typing, doing up buttons.

00:05:51.315 --> 00:05:54.326
If something lifts or cracks, come back to the salon;

00:05:54.595 --> 00:05:56.886
do not peel it off or glue it yourself.

00:05:57.051 --> 00:06:00.806
And book the infill right away, for about three to four weeks later.

00:06:01.077 --> 00:06:02.486
Once the client has gone:

00:06:02.682 --> 00:06:05.126
used paper forms go in a bin with a lid.

00:06:05.384 --> 00:06:08.806
Metal forms are cleaned and disinfected before being used again.

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:12.006
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
